* Generic, literature-based parameter card for fecap_nls (not fitted to any device).
* Generated by fe_models.nls_multidomain.spice_model_card(); keep in sync with GENERIC.
* Instance parameters (put them on the N line): area, s0, sg0.
*   area default 1e-10 m^2 (illustrative (10 um x 10 um))
* FE_ND = 16 domain classes is a compile-time macro (see build_osdi.py).
.model fecap_generic fecap_nls
+ tfe=1e-08
* ^ [m] ferroelectric thickness. Source: illustrative; 8-10 nm is typical of the cited HZO films [Alessandri2018, Alessandri2019]
+ t0=298.15
* ^ [K] reference temperature. Source: 25 C (convention)
+ ps=0.229
* ^ [C/m^2] saturation polarization. Source: P_R = 22.9 uC/cm^2, Table I of [Alessandri2019] (W/HZO 8.3 nm/W)
+ emp=1.775e+08
* ^ [V/m] Dagum scale of the activation field (+ direction). Source: Dagum fit to the GB2 g(E'a) of [Alessandri2019] Table I (a = 12.1, b = 1.79 MV/cm, p = 0.691, q = 0.633)
+ emn=1.775e+08
* ^ [V/m] Dagum scale of the activation field (- direction). Source: same as emp ([Alessandri2019] does not separate polarities)
+ ap=8.68
* ^ [1] Dagum shape (core width), + direction. Source: same Dagum fit as emp
+ an=8.68
* ^ [1] Dagum shape (core width), - direction. Source: same Dagum fit as emp
+ pt=1.136
* ^ [1] Dagum shape; low-field tail G ~ (E/b)^(a p). Source: same Dagum fit as emp; tail exponent a*p = 9.9 (the [Alessandri2018] fit gives about 87)
+ alpha=4.11
* ^ [1] Merz-type exponent. Source: [Alessandri2019] Table I; 3.7-5.5 in [Alessandri2018, AlessandriIEDM2018]
+ beta=2.07
* ^ [1] Weibull exponent (nucleation incubation). Source: [Alessandri2019] Table I; 2.06 in [Alessandri2018]; 2 in [Jo2007]
+ tau0=3.87e-07
* ^ [s] attempt time (tau_inf of the Merz-type law). Source: [Alessandri2019] Table I (387 ns); 236 ns in [Alessandri2018]; strongly device dependent
+ tau_h=3.7e-06
* ^ [s] relaxation time of h without drive. Source: geometric mean of 1.7 us and 8.3 us, the single-exponential times implied by gamma = 0.55 (1 us off) and 0.3 (10 us off) in [Alessandri2019] Eq. 14
+ vimp=-0.08
* ^ [V] built-in (imprint) voltage; loop centre. Source: V_OS = 80 mV in [Alessandri2019] (V_FE = V_A + V_OS)
+ rho=1
* ^ [1] voltage division C_i/(C_i+C_f) by an interface layer. Source: 1 = no interface layer (limit of the charge balance in [Tian2025])
+ vdep=0
* ^ [V] depolarization voltage (back-switching). Source: off by default
+ tau_s=0.0001
* ^ [s] screening time constant. Source: illustrative; inactive while vdep = 0
+ sb=0
* ^ [V] spread of per-class offsets delta_k. Source: off by default
+ c_d=0.02055
* ^ [F/m^2] (1) linear dielectric capacitance (eps_r about 23 at 10 nm). Source: fit of one Lorentzian branch to C-V values read from Fig. 2 (Dev A, TiN/TiN) of [Mukherjee2023EDL]; width from [Mukherjee2023IEDM] Fig. 5a (digitized, approx.)
+ dcap=0.03023
* ^ [F/m^2] (2) peak height of each reversible branch. Source: same fit as c_d
+ frev=1
* ^ [1] instantaneous fraction of term (2). Source: placeholder; the time scale is unresolved in the literature ([Baigol2026] vs [Mukherjee2023IEDM])
+ c_w=0
* ^ [F/m^2] (3) reversible domain-wall capacitance, weighted (1 - x^2). Source: off by default
+ vw=2.236
* ^ [V] half width of each branch. Source: 2.24 MV/cm x 10 nm, from a fit to [Mukherjee2023IEDM] Fig. 5a (digitized, approx.)
+ vs=3.006
* ^ [V] distance of each branch peak from V_i. Source: same fit as c_d (3.0 MV/cm x 10 nm)
+ vi=0
* ^ [V] crossing voltage of the two branches. Source: about 0 for symmetric electrodes ([Mukherjee2023EDL] Dev A)
+ c_r=0
* ^ [F/m^2] state-independent slow capacitance. Source: off by default
+ tau_r=1e-07
* ^ [s] low-pass time constant of y. Source: inactive while frev = 1 and c_w = c_r = 0; order of magnitude from the >2 MHz roll-off of the small-signal window in [Baigol2026] (inference)
+ g_oh=0.0001
* ^ [A/m^2/V] ohmic leakage conductance per area. Source: low-voltage end of the 0-2 V leakage range in [Fehlings2025b] Fig. 6a (digitized, approx.)
+ phi_oh=0
* ^ [eV] activation energy of G_ohm. Source: placeholder (no source found)
+ spf_p=4.8e-12
* ^ [S/m] Poole-Frenkel prefactor, V > 0. Source: scaled so that J(2 V) = 0.1 A/m^2, the upper end of [Fehlings2025b] Fig. 6a (digitized, approx.)
+ spf_n=4.8e-12
* ^ [S/m] Poole-Frenkel prefactor, V < 0. Source: same as spf_p
+ phit_p=0.68
* ^ [eV] Poole-Frenkel trap depth, V > 0. Source: phi_tr,fe = 0.68 eV, Table 1 of [Fehlings2024] (model fit, W/HZO 9.8 nm/W)
+ phit_n=0.68
* ^ [eV] Poole-Frenkel trap depth, V < 0. Source: same as phit_p
+ eps_op=70
* ^ [1] permittivity in the barrier lowering. Source: eps_fe = 70 as used in the PF term of [Fehlings2024]
+ js_p=0
* ^ [A/m^2] Schottky prefactor at T_0, V > 0. Source: off by default
+ js_n=0
* ^ [A/m^2] Schottky prefactor at T_0, V < 0. Source: off by default
+ phib_p=0.48
* ^ [eV] Schottky barrier, V > 0. Source: illustrative; inactive while js_p = 0
+ phib_n=0.48
* ^ [eV] Schottky barrier, V < 0. Source: illustrative; inactive while js_n = 0
+ jt_p=0
* ^ [A/m^2] trap-assisted tunnelling prefactor, V > 0. Source: off by default
+ jt_n=0
* ^ [A/m^2] trap-assisted tunnelling prefactor, V < 0. Source: off by default
+ et_p=1e+09
* ^ [V/m] TAT characteristic field, V > 0. Source: illustrative; inactive while jt_p = 0
+ et_n=1e+09
* ^ [V/m] TAT characteristic field, V < 0. Source: illustrative; inactive while jt_n = 0
+ e0_leak=1e+06
* ^ [V/m] field regularization near 0 V. Source: numerical (10 mV across 10 nm), not a physical quantity
+ tc_ea=0
* ^ [1/K] linear temperature coefficient of the activation field. Source: placeholder (no quantitative source found)
+ tc_ps=0
* ^ [1/K] linear temperature coefficient of P_s. Source: placeholder
+ tc_tau=0
* ^ [1/K] linear temperature coefficient of tau_0. Source: placeholder
+ tc_c=0
* ^ [1/K] linear temperature coefficient of terms (1)+(2). Source: placeholder
+ mul_ps=1
* ^ [1] multiplier on P_s (variation / fatigue hook). Source: hook
+ mul_ea=1
* ^ [1] multiplier on the activation field (variation hook). Source: hook
+ y_max=9
* ^ [1] depth of the logit quantile grid (smallest q about 1.2e-4). Source: numerical
+ grid_a=1.5
* ^ [1] sinh stretching of the quantile grid. Source: numerical
